NAME
    watch - record reads and writes to a memory range without halting

SYNOPSIS
    watch add <space> <addr> <len> [write|read|both]
    watch list
    watch log <id> [<count>]
    watch summary <id>
    watch clear <id>
    watch remove <id>

DESCRIPTION
    Registers live memory watches over hex range <addr>..<addr>+<len>-1 in
    memory space <space> and records matching accesses into a bounded
    event buffer without halting execution. Active watches also appear in
    ps(1) as 'watch<id>' and can be removed with kill(1).

    Read and 'both' watches capture loads only on cores that report read
    hooks and only for spaces where the core publishes load events (for
    example, R3000BUS, RAM, and SCRATCH on PlayStation). On cores without
    read-hook support, a 'read' watch records nothing and a 'both' watch
    records writes only. Each recorded event carries the executing
    instruction address as context.

OPTIONS
    add <space> <addr> <len> [write|read|both]
        Add a watch over <len> hex bytes starting at hex <addr> in <space>
        (default access kind: 'write').

    list
        List active watches with IDs, spaces, address ranges, and access
        kinds.

    log <id> [<count>]
        Show the last <count> recorded (sequence, kind, address, value,
        context) events for watch #<id> (default 20), newest last.

    summary <id>
        Group watch #<id>'s buffered events by access site (PC context)
        with hit counts - the runtime, addressing-mode-agnostic complement
        to readers(1) and writers(1).

    clear <id>
        Clear buffered events for watch #<id> without removing the watch.

    remove <id>
        Remove watch #<id>.

EXAMPLES
    watch add WRAM 13c6 1
    watch add RAM 20000 4 read
    watch list
    watch log 1
    watch summary 1
    watch remove 1

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage/not-found message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    bp(1), framelog(1), counters(1), readers(1), writers(1), spaces(1),
    ps(1), kill(1)
